$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Suzuki Coupling
Reaction. A solution of 4-iodo-chalcogenophene (0.5 mmol) in DMF/H2O
(5:1, 5 mL) was added to a mixture of Pd(PPh3)4 (2 mol %) and K2CO3 (2
equiv). After that, the boronic acid (1.5 equiv) in DMF (0.5 mL) was
added dropwise, and the reaction mixture was stirred under reflux
temperature for 3 h. The organic phase was separated, dried with MgSO4,
and concentrated under vacuum. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography (hexane/ethyl acetate, 98:2).
(4-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-5-phenylthiophen-2-yl)(phenyl)-methanone (7b).
Obtained as a yellow solid. Yield: 0.160 g (86%). mp 113-115 °C. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ (ppm) 7.92-7.90 (m, 2H), 7.64 (s, 1H), 7.59-7.55 (m,
1H), 7.51-7.47 (m, 2H), 7.37-7.33 (m, 2H), 7.30-7.27 (m, 3H), 7.17 (d, J
= 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.81 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 3.78 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3,
100 MHz): δ (ppm) 187.9, 159.0, 146.9, 140.9, 138.8, 138.0, 137.6, 133.4,
132.1, 130.1, 129.1, 129.0, 128.6, 128.5, 128.4, 127.9, 113.9, 55.2. MS
(EI, 70 eV; m/z (relative intensity)): 370 (100), 293 (24), 221 (13), 105
(72), 77 (75). HRMS (ESI-TOF) m/z calcd for C24H18O2S (M + H+): 371.1106,
found: 371.1109.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki Coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diorganyl Dichalcogenides-Promoted Nucleophilic Closure of
1,4-Diyn-3-ols: Synthesis of 2-Benzoyl Chalcogenophenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Roehrs, Juliano A.; Pistoia, Renan P.; Back, Davi F.; Zeni, Gilson
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2015), 80(24), 12470-12481

